  "title": "Pistol Shrimp: The Tiny Animal Louder Than a Gunshot",
  "description": "The pistol shrimp is the size of your finger, yet one snap of its claw can be louder than a gunshot. How does a tiny shrimp make a bang like that?\n\nThe snapping shrimp closes its giant claw so fast that a jet of water tears open a cavitation bubble. When the bubble collapses, it makes the bang that stuns its prey, a tiny flash of light, and, scientists estimate, heat close to the surface of the sun. In World War Two, the crackle of shrimp beds confused Navy sonar, and some reports say submarines hid in the noise.\n\nSubscribe to Stickstory for a strange true story every day. Which animal superpower would you want? Tell me in the comments!\n\n#shorts #pistolshrimp #animalsuperpowers #stickstory",
